Description: The basicstats package contains a few basic statistical functions.
    The MAE function computes the mean absolute error between two sets of data.
    The RMSE function computes the root mean squared error between sets of data.
    The R2 function computes the R-squared between two sets of data.
    The correlation function computes the correlation coefficients between two sets of data using Pearson (default), Spearman or Kendall.
